ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":198,"prev":200,"next":202,"titles":205,"firmware":80},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":28,"procedures":97,"parameters":113,"related":149,"body":154,"sources":155,"official_url":32,"controls":167},"sampler.synth-sampler","Synth sampler",[5,6,7,8,9],"sampler engine","one shot synth sampler","loop points","loop type","record into the synth sampler","sampler",20,"knowledge/manual/units/sampler/synth-sampler.md",{"modes":14,"screens":16},[15],"instrument",[17,18],"M1","sample","Plays one sample across the keyboard. On its record page a keyboard key starts sampling and becomes the root note; `M1` sets start, loop and end points, and its shift layer direction, tune, loop crossfade, gain and loop type.","current",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[24,25],"1.0.45","1.1.0","1.1.15",null,[29,34,37,41,45,49,52,55,58,61,66,69,73,76,82,85,88,92],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"record-key","On the synth sampler's record page you start sampling by pressing a keyboard key; the guide gives this page no `M1` gesture.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#one-shot-synth-sampler","official",{"id":35,"text":36,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"root","The key you press becomes the sample's root, the note the sampler tunes the recording to.",{"id":38,"text":39,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":40},"threshold","The page has the same source, gain and threshold controls as the other record pages (`E1`, `E3`, `E4`), so the key arms the recorder and the take begins once the input passes the threshold.","derived",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":44,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":40},"prompt","TE's picture of this record page reads \"press key to sample\" and labels none of `M1`…`M4`.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#arrange",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":48,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"latch-text","OS 1.0.45 corrected a latch text that the sample screen shows for the synth sampler; the changelog gives no wording, so the prompt on OS 1.1.33 may differ from TE's picture.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.45",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"open","Not documented and not yet checked on a unit — whether `hold M1` also records here, whether the key has to stay held, and what ends a take before 20 seconds.",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"fine","Pushing the encoder in while moving one of the four points gives finer steps.",{"id":56,"text":57,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"no-loop","Loop start at the very end of the sample means no loop.",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"loop-types","Loop forever keeps cycling after release, loop until release stops cycling when you let go, loop off plays straight through.",{"id":62,"text":63,"source":64,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":65},"defaults","After sampling on the unit, the loop runs from 20 % to 80 % of the sample, set to loop forever.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#27-region-fields-by-type","community-verified",{"id":67,"text":68,"source":64,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":65},"ranges","Tune works in cents; sample gain spans −30 to +20 dB.",{"id":70,"text":71,"source":72,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"p-locks","Synth sampler settings accept parameter locks.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.0",{"id":74,"text":75,"source":72,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":27,"confidence":40},"p-lock-values","In the replica a held step locks what `M1` turns, start, loop start, loop end and end, and with `shift` direction, tune, loop crossfade and gain, but not the loop type, which is a click; the changelog does not list them, and they are not yet checked on a unit.",{"id":77,"text":78,"source":79,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":80,"confidence":81},"screen","The page shows an overview strip of the sample on top (base layer only), the left and right waveforms, and start, loop and end markers.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#25-engine-pages-instrument-m1","1.1.33","verified",{"id":83,"text":84,"source":79,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":80,"confidence":81},"shift-screen","With `shift` held it shows direction, tune as a note symbol and a value such as −12.00, crossfade as a percentage drawn as a dark wedge at the loop, and gain.",{"id":86,"text":87,"source":79,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":80,"confidence":81},"no-cc","CC12–15 on the track's channel move nothing on this page.",{"id":89,"text":90,"source":91,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":80,"confidence":81},"crossfade-range","Loop crossfade runs from 0 to 75 %, drawn as a dark wedge sloping down into the loop end over that share of the loop.","docs/research/60-sound-session.md#5-samplers",{"id":93,"text":94,"source":95,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":96},"take-name","A synth sampler take is named after its root note in the project-note-track.wav pattern, for example unnamed-c3-2.wav (community, OS 1.x).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",[98],{"id":99,"goal":100,"preconditions":101,"steps":103,"result":112,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"record","Record a new sample into the synth sampler",[102],"the track uses the synth sampler",[104,106,109],{"keys":18,"note":105,"set":27},"the synth sampler's record page",{"keys":107,"note":108,"set":27},"turn E1","the source; `turn E3` sets the gain and `turn E4` the threshold",{"keys":110,"note":111,"set":27},"key","the note the sample should play at; this starts sampling","The sampler tunes the take to the key you pressed.",[11